==Strategy==
'''Players can hide in Tarn's room just north of the terror dogs and wait for them to develop [[tolerance]] to the player. This makes combating them significantly less risky.''' Be sure to log out to check for tolerance, as any dogs aggressive towards the player will remain so until the player exits Tarn's room, even if all other dogs are no longer aggressive. This will also cause all dogs targeting the player to stop and begin wandering around. Players can check to see if the dogs are still aggressive by exiting Tarn's room and waiting at the door for a quick retreat if they are. 

It is possible to safespot the dogs from Tarn's room using magic or ranged. The dog must be standing on the tile directly in front of the doorway. Walking back and forth between the bookcases in the room while a dog is following you can help position the dog on the correct tile. 

Terror dogs are similar to [[hellhound]]s in that they can hit hard and accurately, but have very low [[Defence]]. As the only area in which they are found is [[multi-combat]], multiple terror dogs can attack at once. Players should be aware that the room that terror dogs are in at Tarn's Lair will drain [[prayer]] at a rate of 1 point per two game ticks, or 50 points per minute (much faster than the [[Barrows]]). Players '''cannot''' set up a cannon in the room.

Fighting terror dogs (mostly done for Slayer tasks) can be a difficult task for players who are unprepared. They can be safespotted if standing in the recesses after they have became tolerant of players.

High-level players, looking to fill the collection log for the [[Granite helm]], may choose to bring their best ranged gear and a [[Venator bow]] to quickly dispatch the Terror dogs. Additionally, a [[Serpentine helm]] and [[Blowpipe]] can be worn initially to tag dogs and lure into the centre, while also inflicting venom. Access to a house rejuvenation pool or the [[Elidinis Statuette]] provides easy restoration while waiting for respawns.

==Transportation==
[[File:Tarn's Lair.png|thumb|400x400px|right|Getting from the Haunted Mine to the terror dogs on foot. Beware of traps!]]
Teleporting to Tarn's Lair via the [[slayer ring]] is the fastest way of reaching to the room with terror dogs. Otherwise, the player will have to get there by foot. The trek to terror dogs is highly dangerous, especially for lower level players. It is recommended to bring high healing foods, [[prayer potion]]s, and possibly dragonhide armour, if the player does not have access to [[Protect from Magic]], as the player will encounter [[Skeleton Mage|Skeleton mage]]s within the lair that casts strong magical attacks at the player.

If the player does not have access to slayer rings, it is possible to navigate [[Tarn's Lair]] manually as shown in the image to the right; [[energy]] management such as a [[stamina potion]] is highly recommended.

